			"updated": 1783427402685,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "In computer science, we don’t measure an algorithm's efficiency in seconds or minutes. \nWhy? \nBecause a program running on a legacy workstation will clock a slower time than the same\nprogram running on a modern high-end machine, even if the code is identical.",
			"rawText": "In computer science, we don’t measure an algorithm's efficiency in seconds or minutes. \nWhy? \nBecause a program running on a legacy workstation will clock a slower time than the same program running on a modern high-end machine, even if the code is identical.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "In computer science, we don’t measure an algorithm's efficiency in seconds or minutes. \nWhy? \nBecause a program running on a legacy workstation will clock a slower time than the same program running on a modern high-end machine, even if the code is identical.",
