			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783427788463,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Option 1: Experimentation\n\nYou could write the code in Java, run it with different data sizes (n), and use\nSystem.currentTimeMillis() to record the average runtimes.\n    Limitations:\n        - You must implement the code first.\n        - Results are skewed by hardware (clock speed, architecture).\n        - Results are skewed by coding style (clean code vs. spaghetti code).\n        - You are only testing limited input sets; it might fail on data you haven't tested.",
			"rawText": "Option 1: Experimentation\n\nYou could write the code in Java, run it with different data sizes (n), and use System.currentTimeMillis() to record the average runtimes.\n    Limitations:\n        - You must implement the code first.\n        - Results are skewed by hardware (clock speed, architecture).\n        - Results are skewed by coding style (clean code vs. spaghetti code).\n        - You are only testing limited input sets; it might fail on data you haven't tested.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "vCb5Mz21",
			"originalText": "Option 1: Experimentation\n\nYou could write the code in Java, run it with different data sizes (n), and use System.currentTimeMillis() to record the average runtimes.\n    Limitations:\n        - You must implement the code first.\n        - Results are skewed by hardware (clock speed, architecture).\n        - Results are skewed by coding style (clean code vs. spaghetti code).\n        - You are only testing limited input sets; it might fail on data you haven't tested.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
