			"versionNonce": 2025496120,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783431571834,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Growth Rate: Refers to the increase in runtime as size (n) increases. We always look for\nthe fastest-growing term.\n  - Example A: Time is proportional to n (Linear rate).\n  - Example B: Time is proportional to n² (Quadratic rate).",
			"rawText": "Growth Rate: Refers to the increase in runtime as size (n) increases. We always look for the fastest-growing term.\n  - Example A: Time is proportional to n (Linear rate).\n  - Example B: Time is proportional to n² (Quadratic rate).",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "57jkne1t",
			"originalText": "Growth Rate: Refers to the increase in runtime as size (n) increases. We always look for the fastest-growing term.\n  - Example A: Time is proportional to n (Linear rate).\n  - Example B: Time is proportional to n² (Quadratic rate).",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
